# Endpoint file for lesscode-model, which makes every model call of lesscode
# (regenerate run, the guide optimiser). docs/model-endpoint.md has the details.
# Copy to a file outside the repository, or to .env here, fill in the key, and
# name the file in one of three ways:
#   lesscode-model check --endpoint-env FILE
#   $env:LESSCODE_MODEL_ENV = "$PWD\.env"      (PowerShell)
#   export LESSCODE_MODEL_ENV="$PWD/.env"      (sh)
# Without either, %USERPROFILE%\.lesscode\model.env (~/.lesscode/model.env) is read.
# Then check it:   lesscode-model check
# .env is git-ignored. Never commit a real key.

# Mistral (OpenAI-compatible chat completions)
LESSCODE_MODEL_API_STYLE=openai
LESSCODE_MODEL_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
LESSCODE_MODEL_NAME=mistral-large-4
LESSCODE_MODEL_API_KEY=replace-with-your-key
# Optional: the reasoning level, sent as reasoning_effort to an OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
# LESSCODE_MODEL_REASONING_EFFORT=high
#
# LESSCODE_MODEL_NAME and LESSCODE_MODEL_REASONING_EFFORT can also be set in the
# environment of one run; a value set there stands before the one in this file:
#   $env:LESSCODE_MODEL_NAME = "another-model"

# Anthropic (Messages API) instead:
# LESSCODE_MODEL_API_STYLE=anthropic
# LESSCODE_MODEL_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
# LESSCODE_MODEL_NAME=claude-opus-5-5
# LESSCODE_MODEL_API_KEY=replace-with-your-key